+      "exact_boundary": "The source states an in-principle terminating interval-enclosure METHOD for the explicit collision expression C_alg(d,L) at fixed finite d >= 2 and computable L > 0 with certified interval access, using the full spectrum with analytic tails (line 20). Its components are: uniform covariance floors (M5)-(M13); certified moment tails at positive integer cutoffs (M14)-(M15); guarded charts and frames (M16)-(M19); the cone-weight Lipschitz Lemma |w(A) - w(B)| <= 2nR^{2n-1}||A - B||_op (lines 240-244); a Cholesky Gaussian representation with an explicit Gaussian-tail remainder (M22)-(M27); and a box-integration scheme whose output interval contains C_alg with width <= epsilon (lines 330-335). It also states the conditional estimate (M30) (lines 354-359). No literal Lean kernel declaration states any of these at this cut. The paper proof, the analytic controls of section 12 and the scoped method acceptances are not admitted as closure, and no enclosure has been executed. Named open items: G1-G4 and an M31-type finite-ell bound are needed to identify C_alg with the barcode leading coefficient; M30's application needs the pin-covariance floor and same-field convergence premises; and faithful outward interval arithmetic is assumed, not verified. Not vacuous.",
