+      "source_statements": [
+        {
+          "line_start": 20,
+          "line_end": 20,
+          "text": "Call the right side of the original equation (1) C_alg(d,L). The result of this unit is a finite, in-principle terminating interval-enclosure METHOD for C_alg at the ORIGINAL fixed finite d>=2 and L>0, once d is given and L is supplied as a computable positive real with certified interval access. It uses the full original spectrum, with analytically bounded omitted sums. It does not replace the covariance by a cutoff field, replace L by infinity, remove the zero mode, or change height conditioning."
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 240,
+          "line_end": 244,
+          "text": "**Lemma.** For real symmetric n by n matrices A,B with operator norms at most R,\n\n\\[\n|w(A)-w(B)|\\le 2n R^{2n-1}\\|A-B\\|_{\\rm op},\\qquad n\\ge1.\\tag{M20}\n\\]"
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 330,
+          "line_end": 335,
+          "text": "A concrete certificate-producing scheme is therefore:\n\n1. Obtain certified intervals for the ACTUAL fixed positive L, pi and the finite sums in M14 at positive integer cutoff M, with outward tails M15. Enclose a,b,c; compute strict floors from M12–M13 and the bounds in Section 3. If an interval floor remains nonpositive, refine it or use the positive witness bounds. Do not infer positivity from a floating midpoint.\n2. For a requested absolute coefficient tolerance epsilon>0, choose a POSITIVE INTEGER Gaussian radius R with the certified upper bound in M27 <=epsilon/3. This is possible because that bound tends to zero along the positive integers; no sample/model computation is needed.\n3. With the positive integer R from Step 2, partition each compact (x,z) rectangle into finitely many boxes with rational endpoints and hence exact rational volumes. On each box enclose e,U,B,Gamma,L_e,V,J and phi_N by outward interval operations. Use M21 with a rational matrix center to enclose w, then multiply the nonnegative factor intervals. Sum each interval times its exact rational box volume, and sum faces. Let the resulting truncated-integral interval be [ell_R,u_R]. All moment and elementary-function uncertainties remain inside this interval.\n4. Refine the moment/input/constant intervals and box partitions until u_R-ell_R<=2epsilon/3. Output [ell_R,u_R+E_G^upper(R)]. The true C_alg lies in this interval, whose width is <=epsilon."
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 354,
+          "line_end": 359,
+          "text": "One precise limited implication is available. Let X be the actual centered Gaussian field as a random element of its physical Sobolev Hilbert space H^k, with M_k=E||X||_(H^k)^2<infinity. Let Y be a finite centered Gaussian pin vector with covariance Sigma>=lambda I>0. Gaussian Hilbert-space regression yields\n\n\\[\nE[\\|X\\|_{H^k}^2\\mid Y=y]\n \\le M_k(1+|y|^2/\\lambda).\\tag{M30}\n\\]"
+        }
