+      "source_statements": [
+        {
+          "line_start": 132,
+          "line_end": 134,
+          "text": "**Lemma F₃ (the fold layer at order `r`).** For every `k > 0` and `u`,\n\n    lim_{r↓0} (𝐓_r(k, u) − 𝐒_r(k, u))/r = 𝐋_F(k, u).                                                              (F₃)"
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 136,
+          "line_end": 137,
+          "text": "**Lemma T₁ (the cusp tail).** For every `u`, `lim_{κ→∞} κ(𝓐(κ, u) − 𝐀₂(0, u)) = a₁(u)`. Moreover `a₁(u) = (1/10)∫_RF₀(b, u)db`,\nwith `F₀` as in #242 (1.0)."
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 139,
+          "line_end": 143,
+          "text": "**Theorem C3 (the `ℓ^{2/3}` term of the candidate density).** In every `d ≥ 2` and for every `L`, `|𝐄(k, u)| ≤ C min(k, 1/k)`\nfor `k > 0`, and as `ℓ ↓ 0`\n\n    ν_cand(ℓ) = c ℓ^{−1/3} + B_{d,L} + I^{cand} ℓ^{1/4} + c₂ ℓ^{1/3} + c₃ ℓ^{2/3} + o(ℓ^{2/3}),\n    c₃ := (1/3) ∫_{S^{d−1}} ∫_0^∞ 𝐄(k, u) k^{−5/3} dk dσ(u).                                                       (C3)"
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 145,
+          "line_end": 155,
+          "text": "**Proposition G (the Gaussian kernel).** Let `C(z) = e^{−|z|²/2}` on `R^d` (the model case of #242 §0), `d ≥ 2`, and\nevaluate (0.3) and (C3) on the model's jet law. Then:\n- (G.1) For every `k` and every unit `e ⊥ u`, under `Q̄_{0,k}` the pair `(γ_e, B_ee)` is independent of `A`, and its law is that\n  of two independent `N(0, 2)` variables, not depending on `k`. Moreover `p_{V_0}(v(k)) = e^{−12k²}p_{V_0}(v(0))`.\n- (G.2) Put `g(k) := E|3kB − γ²/4|³` for independent `γ, B ~ N(0, 2)`. Then `g(0) = 15/8` and\n  `𝐄(k, u) = (a₁/k)(e^{−12k²}g(k)/g(0) − 1)`, with `a₁ = (1/10)∫F₀db` independent of `u`.\n- (G.3) `c₃ = (J/30)∫_{S^{d−1}}∫_RF₀ db dσ`, where\n\n      J := ∫_0^∞ (e^{−12k²}g(k)/g(0) − 1) k^{−8/3} dk = (16/15) ∫_0^∞ e^{−12k²} E[(3kB − γ²/4)₊³] k^{−8/3} dk > 0.        (G)\n\n  With #242's Corollary 1′, `c₃ = J·5√3/(288π²)` in `d = 2` and `c₃ = J·25√30/(1152π³)` in `d = 3`."
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 157,
+          "line_end": 160,
+          "text": "**Corollary G′ (the model value is positive).** For the Gaussian kernel, the coefficient `c₃` of (C3), evaluated on the\nmodel's jet law, is positive. By Theorem C3, for any field to which it applies and whose `c₃` is nonzero, the remainder\n`O(ℓ^{2/3})` of note LU's Theorem P⁺ is of exact order `ℓ^{2/3}`. Theorems P⁺ and C3 are stated for the torus field of #237\n§0; Proposition G″ transfers the sign to it for large `L`."
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 162,
+          "line_end": 165,
+          "text": "**Proposition G″ (the torus field for large `L`).** Let `c₃(L)` be the coefficient (C3) of the torus field of side `L`\n(#237 §0). Then `c₃(L) → (J/30)∫_{S^{d−1}}∫_RF₀ db dσ` as `L → ∞`, with the model's `F₀`. Hence there is `L₀(d)` such that,\nfor `L ≥ L₀(d)`, `c₃(L) > 0`, and the remainder `O(ℓ^{2/3})` of note LU's Theorem P⁺ is of exact order `ℓ^{2/3}` for the\ntorus field. `L₀(d)` is not quantified here."
