+      "source_hypotheses": "Setting and notation of #237 §§0-2 and note LU §0 (lines 100-110): m = d − 1, s := (−1)^m; pins M = −ru/2, S = ru/2; rows V_r, target v(k) = (0_d, 0_d, 12k), density p_{V_r} and law Q̄_{r,k} (#237 (1.1)); scaled endpoint Hessians K_M, K_S and Π; kernel 𝐓_r and fixed-cone surrogate 𝐒_r (#237 (R.1)); 𝐀_0, 𝐀₂ (Lemma K), 𝓐(κ, u) and κ = k/r; jets A, B, γ, f₄ with Δ, A^♯, Δ_B, Y′, U, V; constants depending only on d and L. Edge objects (0.1)-(0.3) (lines 112-126): the eigenvalues of A are simple almost surely; P, B_ee, γ_e, U_red; the edge expectation 𝔼_Q[φ; λ_m = 0⁻] defined as a limit when it exists; 𝔏, 𝐋_F, a₁ and 𝐄. Theorem C3: every d ≥ 2 and every L, for the torus field of #237 §0 (lines 139, 159-160). Proposition G: the model kernel C(z) = e^{−|z|²/2} on R^d, d ≥ 2, with (0.3) and (C3) evaluated on the model's jet law (lines 145-146). Proposition G″: c₃(L) of the torus field of side L; parity-split jet covariances θ in a compact neighbourhood 𝒩 of θ_∞ on which all covariances are uniformly nondegenerate (lines 406-414); the periodization estimate O(L⁶e^{−L²/2}) for derivatives of order at most 6 (lines 426-428). Lemma F₃ is stated for every k > 0 and u (line 132), Lemma T₁ for every u (line 136), (G.1) for every k and every unit e ⊥ u (line 147); J uses γ, B independent N(0, 2) (lines 39, 149). Corollary G′'s exact-order conclusion is stated for any field to which Theorem C3 applies and whose c₃ is nonzero (lines 158-159).",
